## 7. Recommended architecture

**LVGL 8.3 (pinned) as the render/widget layer, inside a bespoke Totoro shell and session layer, rendering at 120×160 logical, 2× integer-scaled, RGB565 internally, with dirty-row flush via `0x46ff`.**

```
Android (host, preserved, always recoverable)
├─ totoro-session                 ← Android-side supervisor (su/sh)
│    stop bootanim → SystemUI → system_server → zygote → surfaceflinger
│    VT to KD_GRAPHICS; backlight on; disable suspend/timeout
│    exec totoro-shell inside the ext2 chroot
│    watchdog: exit | SIGUSR1 | hard timeout | forced-abort tap  →  restore Android
└─ Linux userspace (musl, static, SD-backed ext2 rootfs)
   ├─ totoro-fb        mmap fb0, back page, RGB565→888 expand, dirty-row0x46ff, 30 Hz pacing
   ├─ totoro-ts        evdev /dev/input/event4, calibration, tap/swipe/long-press, 4-button row
   ├─ totoro-shell     YOUR shell: view stack, launcher grid, status bar, soft buttons
   ├─ tui/             toolkit-independent interface
   │    ├─ backend_lvgl     (default)
   │    └─ backend_basic    (~1.5 kLOC immediate-mode fallback)
   ├─ apps/            files, terminal (libvterm+busybox pty), settings, about/recovery, micropython
   └─ dropbear         always-on control + recovery channel
```

**Key LVGL v8.3 configuration:** `LV_COLOR_DEPTH 16` · `LV_MEM_SIZE` 65536 · partial draw buffer sized to ~40 logical rows · `LV_DISP_DEF_REFR_PERIOD` 30 · disable shadow, gradient, antialias, and every unused widget/anim · custom `LV_THEME_DEFAULT` with 1px bevels, radius 0, period palette · one embedded 8×8 bitmap font converted to an `lv_font_t` · custom `flush_cb` → `totoro-fb` · custom `read_cb` → `totoro-ts`.

**Render scale:** 120×160 logical at 2× gives you 240×320 physical exactly. A bottom taskbar/soft-button row occupies ~20 logical rows; the viewport above it is a 120×140 play area — a pleasant, chunky, believable handheld.

